# Retirement account types

Tax-deferred accounts stay `kind: "retirementTaxable"` (RMDs, conversions, and
ordinary-income tax are unchanged). The picker is `Account.retirementType`:

`401k` | `403b` | `457b` | `ira` | `tsp` | `drop`

Labels live in `RETIREMENT_ACCOUNT_TYPE_LABELS` / `RETIREMENT_ACCOUNT_TYPES`
(`household.ts`). Do not re-declare them in the UI or `planDiff`.

## Migration

Older plans have no subtype. `migrateHousehold` / `healRetirementType` set
missing or unknown values to `"drop"` on live accounts and `deletedAccounts`.
New cards default to DROP too. Strip `retirementType` from any other kind.

## Growth start (DROP delay)

Every account card has a **Growth starts** toggle (`Account.growthStart`):
`planStart` ("Plan start") compounds from today, `retirement` ("Retirement")
stays flat until the owner's `retirementYear` and first grows in that year.
Unset means the type default (`defaultGrowthStart`): `retirement` for DROP,
`planStart` for everything else. Read it through `accountGrowthStart`, never
`growthStart` directly. `healGrowthStart` renames the old `afterRetirement`
value (which grew from the year after retiring) to `retirement` and drops
unknown values. If the owner has no retirement year, fall back to the
household start year (`accountGrowsInYear`). Joint accounts use `ownerId`.

Example: plan starts 2030 (David), Batsheva retires 2032. Her DROP is flat in
2030 and 2031. First 5% is 2032. Her IRA still grows in 2030 (and from today
up to 2030) unless it's switched to Retirement.

`projectScenario` and `convertibleTotal` both call `accountGrowsInYear`. Keep
them in sync. Pre-start deposits into a `retirement` account add principal only
(`preStartDepositValue` uses rate 0): growth never starts before the plan
does, and in-loop deposits still land after the grow step, so such a deposit
in the retirement year first compounds the following year.

A `planStart` balance is as of today (`refs.asOfDate`): `openingBalance`
compounds it up to January 1 of the start year when today is earlier, and
year 0 grows only the rest of the year when today falls in it. See "RMDs are
set by law" in `AGENTS.md`.
